From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 05:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(web): open items behind a button in the session header

The Open items bar takes a full-width row above every transcript that uses
item labels, whether or not the reader wants the list right now, and it has
no room to grow into more than a list of items.

The list now opens from a compact button in the session header, beside
Agent info, sized and named like the other header buttons. Its badge is the
number of open items (closed and dismissed ones left out). Clicking it
opens a popover on desktop; on a phone it opens a sheet docked to the
bottom of the screen. The panel holds the tracker itself, expanded: the
same chips, titles, latest-reply grouping, Closed fold, dismiss and restore,
and each item's preview with "Show in conversation", which closes the panel
so the message it jumps to is not covered.

The transcript still derives the items, so it owns the button and portals
it into a slot the header provides (one line in ChatHeader). OpenItemsPanel
gains a "section" layout for use inside another panel instead of being
copied. Where a transcript is shown without the session header there is no
slot, and the pinned bar stays as before.

Nothing is stored: as with the bar, the items are read from the loaded
transcript, so an item mentioned only in history that has not been loaded
is missing until the reader scrolls up to it.

Phone sheet placement and the look of the badge are covered by unit tests
and reading only; no browser run was made.

Local only: this extends the chat-item-labels series (the open-items
tracker), which is not upstream, and is not proposed upstream yet.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
